139535560 true] [17592186355171 1100 "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x}\\le 3\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355171 1113 #uuid "b94169f1-377c-5964-ba3c-f879e9c9f359" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355171 1145 "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x} & \\le 9\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{x}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{5}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, note that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$ is a negative quantity, so when we divide both sides by it, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355173 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355174 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355175 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355176 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355177 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1041 "selection" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186355176 13194139535560 true] [17592186355172 1110 #uuid "d60c77db-f966-5c7a-93a6-10618646dc03" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355173 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535560 true] [17592186355173 1111 #uuid "cae78912-b81d-555d-8d98-6f257b499c47" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355174 1034 "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535560 true] [17592186355174 1111 #uuid "7c68af60-ec46-574b-82f2-e0664a4d68b9" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355175 1034 "x\\le \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535560 true] [17592186355175 1111 #uuid "f958928b-8f25-5bd0-b4cb-5892c64e7e0d" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355176 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535560 true] [17592186355176 1111 #uuid "a78770ef-3fe3-56f7-9c05-e4d09d459051" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355177 1034 "x\\ge \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535560 true] [17592186355177 1111 #uuid "cc07a8a9-56ee-5707-a5b9-146513dfeeaa" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355179 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1089 "q-87731" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1100 "Solve the inequality ${(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x+4}-3\\le 1.$" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1113 #uuid "1b3c40d0-95c1-536f-a37b-d489b8751edb" 13194139535560 true] [17592186355178 1145 "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x+4}-3 & \\le 1 \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x+4} & \\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x+4}] & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ (x+4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{3}) & \\le \\operatorn